<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A({-1},\,{-1},\,{-4})</m>, <m>B({-3},\,{-3},\,{-2})</m> and <m>C(s,\,{-5},\,t)</m> are collinear, with <m>\overrightarrow{AC} = k\,\overrightarrow{AB}</m>. Fractions are fine; type a fraction with a slash, for example 5/3.</p><div>(a) <m>k =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans1"/>  </div><div>(b) <m>s =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/>  </div><div>(c) <m>t =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans3"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p><m>\overrightarrow{AB} = {\left(\begin{array}{c} -2 \\ -2 \\ 2 \end{array}\right)}</m> and <m>\overrightarrow{AC} = \begin{pmatrix} s - ({-1}) \\ \displaystyle{-4} \\ t - ({-4}) \end{pmatrix}</m>.</p><p>(a) The y-components are both known: <m>{-4} = k \times ({-2})</m>, so <m>k = {2}</m>.</p><p>(b) <m>s = {-1} + k \times ({-2}) = {-5}</m>.</p><p>(c) <m>t = {-4} + k \times ({2}) = {0}</m>.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>2</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>-5</m></p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>0</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>